// Drive-time isochrones from Faith Church, one per 5-minute step from 5 to 60.
//
// Computed with the local OSRM (eastern-PA extract, v5.26.0): radial probes on
// 144 bearings, the farthest point still reachable within each threshold.
// Rings are [lng, lat] (GeoJSON order), open — the renderer closes them.
// 288 vertices each (a point every ~0.65 km on the 30-minute ring), halved
// from the 576 probed because this module ships to the browser with the map
// page and the extra precision was invisible at valley zoom.
//
// SMOOTHED IN POLAR SPACE, NOT IN X/Y. The first attempt used Chaikin
// smoothing on the polygon, which cuts corners off a spiky ring harder than a
// smooth one — and that let the 50- and 55-minute rings dip INSIDE the ring
// below them, so the map would have said 50 minutes reaches less far than 45.
// Smoothing the radius as a function of bearing cannot do that: the filter has
// non-negative weights and is applied identically at every threshold, so if the
// raw radii nest, the smoothed radii nest. Verified: every ring now encloses
// the one below it, and the church sits inside all twelve.
//
// PRECOMPUTED ON PURPOSE. OSRM is not kept running — this host has 954 MB of
// RAM and the app was being OOM-killed until recently, so a routing daemon
// holding ~260 MB is not something to leave up for a map overlay. It was
// started once, all twelve rings were generated in ~2 minutes, and the
// container was removed.
//
// TO REGENERATE WITHOUT OSRM: fc-isochrones-raw.json holds the raw reach in km
// per bearing per threshold. Re-smoothing from that needs no routing at all.
// Only a change in the road network needs OSRM again; the prepared extract is
// still at /home/ubuntu/osrm on the server (run osrm/osrm-backend:latest — the
// current :latest image cannot read data built by v5.26).
export type IsoRing = ReadonlyArray<readonly [number, number]>;

/** The drive times we hold a ring for, in minutes. */
export const ISO_MINUTES = [5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40, 45, 50, 55, 60] as const;
export type IsoMinutes = (typeof ISO_MINUTES)[number];

/** The default the campus planner opens on. */
export const ISO_DEFAULT_MINUTES = 30;

